Package: mc-mgmt
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: any
Maintainer: Dylan Bulmer <dylan@bulmer.dev>
Depends: mc-server (>= 1.0.0), ${shlibs:Depends}
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://apt.bulmer.dev
Description: Management protocol console plugin for mc-server
 Adds the 'mc mgmt' subcommand and the lifecycle hooks that make a shutdown
 graceful and a backup consistent, speaking the Minecraft Server Management
 Protocol — JSON-RPC over a WebSocket, served by the game itself from Minecraft
 1.21.9 onwards. Older servers do not offer it.
 .
 Where the server is new enough this is the better console. Authentication is a
 bearer token rather than a plaintext password shared with every client, and the
 interface is a typed API with structured results rather than console command
 strings whose output has to be scraped, so a player list is a list and a failed
 call is an error instead of a blank reply.
 .
 Installing this alongside mc-rcon is correct and safe. Both register as console
 providers and mc elects one per server: it prefers this plugin, but only after
 asking it whether the management endpoint is actually reachable, and falls back
 to RCON on any server that cannot answer. A mixed fleet of old and new servers
 needs no per-host configuration.
 .
 The plugin declares mc's ABI version in its manifest, so an incompatible pair
 of packages is refused by name rather than failing at run time.
